  {"title": "Single parity check",
   "body": r"<p>The \((n,n-1)\) single-parity-check code is the set of sequences of \(n\) bits with an even number of ones. Give \(H\), a systematic \(G\), the minimum distance and the rate. What does ML decoding do on the BEC when one bit is erased? On the BSC, what are the two cosets, and what are their leaders? What can the decoder do when the syndrome is \(1\)?</p>"},
